{% comment %}
  Setup hint — shown inside a section when it has no real store data yet, so the
  preview renders sample/mock content PLUS a clear instruction of what the
  merchant must create in Shopify (collection, menu, products…). Once they create
  it and pick it, the real data replaces the mock automatically.
  Usage: {% render 'setup-note', message: 'Create a collection and select it here.' %}
  Styles live in assets/store.css (.setup-note) so this works in any section.
{% endcomment %}
{%- if message != blank -%}
  <div class="setup-note" role="note">
    <span class="setup-note__badge">Setup</span>
    <span class="setup-note__msg">{{ message }}{% if action_url != blank %} <a class="setup-note__link" href="{{ action_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Shopify admin →</a>{% endif %}</span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
